1.2.4 Thermal homeostasis: ecto-, homeo- & endothermy
Temperature affects metabolic rates, cf {16}, so control over metabolic rates requires control over body temperature. Heat is a side product of all uses of energy, cf. {155}. In ectotherms, this heat simply dissipates without increasing the body temperature above that of the environment to any noticeable amount as long as the temperature is sufficiently


