2.5.4 Reproduction overhead
Since embryos initially exist almost exclusively of reserve, the allocation to reproduction consists of reserve, and the strong homeostasis assumption makes that reserve cannot change in composition, little metabolic work is involved in reproduction. Yet some work is involved in the conversion of (part of) the buffer of reserve that is allocated to reproduction into eggs. A fraction κR of the reproduction flux, called the reproduction efficiency, is assumed to be fixed in embryo reserve, and the rest, a fraction 1−κR is used as reproduction overhead.
